course: dictionary
lesson: 8653
title: Seashore: a place word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A seashore is the land along the edge of the sea, such as a beach, rocks or sand. The word is made of two parts, sea and shore. A shore is the edge of land next to water, so the seashore is the shore by the sea.
explain: Seashore can also mean the area between high tide and low tide. «The seashore is a harder home, because twice a day the tide goes out and leaves rockpool animals in sun, wind and beaks.» The tide goes out, so the seashore is the ground that is uncovered between the tides.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. Limpets clamp down, anemones fold into blobs of jelly and crabs hide under weed: these are animals that live there. Clues like these show that the seashore is a habitat, a place where living things make their home.
fact: Seashore is a noun: «the seashore», «seashores».
fact: «Seashore» means the land along the edge of the sea, such as a beach, rocks or sand.
fact: The seashore is the area between high tide and low tide.
fact: «Seashore creatures» are animals that live on the seashore, such as crabs, limpets and seabirds.
fact: Rock pools form on the seashore, and the tide leaves animals in them when it goes out.
exercise: What is the seashore? | A ship that sails along the coast | A deep part of the ocean where no light reaches | *The land along the edge of the sea, such as a beach or rocks | A road that runs past the sea
exercise: Find the area that lies between high tide and low tide. | The harbour wall | *The seashore | The sea bed | The cliff top
exercise: In «crabs hide under weed», which word is an animal? | weed | hide | *crabs | under
test: Why does the seashore change twice a day? | Because the wind stops | *Because the tide goes out and comes back in | Because children walk on it | Because the sun moves across the sky
test: Which word means a place where living things make their home? | blob | *habitat | tide | noun
exam: Jayden says, «The seashore is the same as the sea.» What is wrong with this? | Nothing is wrong | The seashore is always underwater | The seashore is only sand | *The seashore is land by the sea, not the sea itself
